findings.body:
The comment-only branch of `reviewDigest` treats "no open thread" as clean:

```ts
if (status?.state === 'PENDING' && status.description.startsWith(COMMENT_ONLY_STATUS)) {
  return line(`skipped, a comment-only push (${said})`, threads, threads,
    threads > 0 ? "comment `@claude review` …" : "ready for the operator's merge click");
}
```

The SUCCESS branch requires the exact status `no blocking issues` before it says ready, and decision 90 says the same: next is "`ready for the operator's merge click` under the clean full-review status, and otherwise reading the PR". A comment-only skip is not that status, and its description (`Not reviewed: only comments and prose changed since <sha7>`) carries no verdict; the earlier review's status sits on an older commit that `readPullRequestReview` never reads.

Reachable paths:
1. **No attacker needed.** `post-review.script.ts` (L103-104, L228-233) sends a finding with no anchor to the review body and still counts it, so head A gets SUCCESS `1 important finding(s)` with 0 threads; `pup ci wait` correctly says "read the PR". A comment-only push follows; the preflight skips any comment-only delta after a complete record regardless of its findings (`newestCleanRecord` only drops errored/partial records) and posts the PENDING skip. `pup ci wait` now prints `0 open thread(s), 0 important → ready for the operator's merge click`.
2. **Worker-shaped.** In a `pup fix` round the worker edits only a comment in the threads' file and answers `fixed`; the round's commit touched that file, so the threads are resolved; the push is comment-only, so the head gets the skip and the digest reads ready. The conductor's `CI_REVIEW_LOOP` then reports the PR ready for the merge click although no one reviewed or fixed the important findings.

The operator's click still gates the merge, but this is the signal the loop exists to give them. Suggested fix: on the skip with no open thread, name "read the PR" (this head was not reviewed and the earlier verdict isn't read) instead of ready, or read the prior review's status before saying ready; `ci-wait.test.ts`'s comment-only case (L233-245) expects "ready" and would need updating.

